WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.963
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module.

2
00:00:02.963 --> 00:00:07.087
Name the prevention settings that have
an audit mode, and the ones that don't.

3
00:00:07.087 --> 00:00:11.965
Move network protection and controlled
folder access from audit to block,

4
00:00:11.965 --> 00:00:15.426
ring by ring, with exit
criteria and backout triggers.

5
00:00:15.426 --> 00:00:19.907
Run every Attack Surface Reduction rule
through audit and warn into block,

6
00:00:19.907 --> 00:00:22.075
and name the two rules that skip warn.

7
00:00:22.075 --> 00:00:26.725
Record per-rule exclusions, and
prefer an exclusion to a step back.

8
00:00:26.725 --> 00:00:31.537
And verify each setting on the device, and
read the fleet's audit and block events.

9
00:00:31.537 --> 00:00:35.000
You need Module 1, so the
ring's devices are onboarded.

10
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.847
Skim the Devices and Endpoints book's
policies E S oh-oh-one for antivirus,

11
00:00:39.847 --> 00:00:44.936
E S oh-oh-three for the firewall, and E S
oh-oh-five for Attack Surface Reduction:

12
00:00:44.936 --> 00:00:47.925
the setting values live
there, not in the guide.

13
00:00:47.925 --> 00:00:51.340
Lab 2 runs in a test
tenant, never production.
